Anya P: Quick sync — PR #4611 touches SDK snippets across Python/TypeScript/Go. We shipped the new streaming iterator and renamed pagination tokens. Need: minimal migration blurb + tiny copy-paste examples for each language. Who can pick up which language?
Carlos D: I got TS. Will swap event/callback patterns for the async iterator and show brief error handling (retry note will be separate). Will also scan for broken anchors.
Mei L: I'll handle Python. Thinking an async iterator example plus a compact async retry helper using asyncio.sleep. Will include a one-line "don't retry 4xx" note.
Sam W: I'll take Go. Plan: show old Chunks()/OnData -> new StreamIter() pattern and a one-line pagination mapping. I'll keep snippets 8 lines or less.
Nina K: docs-bot flagged a broken link in the original PR: /docs/streams_old -> 404.
Anya P: Replace with /docs/streams and add migration sentence: "page -> page_token, per_page -> page_size; responses now include next_page_token." Also add: "Prefer short, capped retries on 5xx/timeouts; do not retry 4xx." Keep the migration blurb to one short paragraph.
Sam W: Go snippet (pre/post):
```go
// pre-migration
resp, _ := client.Stream(ctx, req)
for c := range resp.Chunks() { fmt.Println(c.Text) }

// post-migration
it := client.StreamIter(ctx, req)
for it.Next() { fmt.Println(it.Value().Text) }
```
Mei L: Python async draft (compact retry + iterator):
```py
import asyncio

async def tiny_retry(fn, tries=3):
    for i in range(tries):
        try:
            return await fn()
        except TransientError:
            await asyncio.sleep(min(2**i, 5))
    raise

async with client.stream_iter(prompt) as it:
    async for chunk in it:
        print(chunk.text)
# note: avoid retrying on 4xx
```
Carlos D: TypeScript example (switch from events to async iterator):
```ts
// old: event listeners
const s = client.stream(req)
s.on('data', c => console.log(c.text))

// new: async iterator
try {
  for await (const chunk of client.streamIter(req)) {
    console.log(chunk.text)
  }
} catch (err) {
  // handle/propagate transient vs client errors
}
```
